          %h2#references References
          %h3#general General
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riccardo+D%27Auria"}> Riccardo D'Auria
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pietro+Fr%C3%A9"} Pietro Fré
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Geometric structure of
                    = succeed "," do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi N
                            %mo =
                            %mn 1
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N=1
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi D
                          %mo =
                          %mn 10
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D=10
                    and
                    = succeed "," do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi N
                            %mo =
                            %mn 4
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N=4
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi D
                          %mo =
                          %mn 4
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D=4
                    super Yang-Mills theory
                %strong 196
                2 (1982) 205-239 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0550-3213(82)90036-0"}> doi:10.1016/0550-3213(82)90036-0
                \&amp;rbrack;
              %blockquote
                %p
                  (in
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%27Auria-Fr%C3%A9+formulation+of+supergravity"} D'Auria-Fré formulation
          %p
            Discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%3D4+N%3D4+SYM"} D=4 N=4 SYM
            with emphasis on
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multi-trace+operators"} multi-trace operators
          %ul
            %li
              P. J. Heslop,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Howe"} Paul Howe
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  Aspects of
                  = succeed "=4" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝒩
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{N}
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0307210"} arXiv:hep-th/0307210
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superconformal+group"} Superconformal
            invariance of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒩
                    %mo =
                    %mn 4
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{N}=4
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                  %mo =
                  %mn 4
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D=4
            SYM can be shown with the result of
          %ul
            %li
              Robert Leigh,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Matthew+Strassler"} Matthew Strassler
              %em
                Exactly Marginal Operators and Duality in Four Dimensional
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒩
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{N}=1
                Supersymmetric Gauge Theory
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9503121"}> arXiv:hep-th/9503121
              )
          %p
            (after regarding it as
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒩
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{N}=1
            SYM with three adjoint chiral
            = succeed "s)." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superfield"} superfield
          %p
            Introductions in view of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/single+trace+operators"} single trace operators
            as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+chain"} spin chain
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integrable+systems"} integrable systems
            in the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS%2FCFT+correspondence"} AdS/CFT correspondence
          %ul
            %li
              Joseph A. Minahan
              %em
                Review of AdS/CFT Integrability, Chapter I.1: Spin Chains in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒩
                      %mo =
                      %mn 4
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{N}=4
                Super Yang-Mills
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1012.3983"}> arXiv:1012.3983
              )
          %p More recent results are in
          %ul
            %li
              Simon Caron-Huot,
              %em Superconformal symmetry and two-loop amplitudes in planar N=4 super Yang-Mills
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1105.5606"}> arXiv:1105.5606
              )
          %h3#matrix_model_description Matrix model description
          %p
            On the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BMN+matrix+model"} BMN matrix model
            as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-compactification"} KK-compactification
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%3D4+N%3D4+super+Yang-Mills+theory"} D=4 N=4 super Yang-Mills theory
            on the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/3-sphere"} 3-sphere
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nakwoo+Kim"}> Nakwoo Kim
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomas+Klose"} Thomas Klose
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jan+Plefka"} Jan Plefka
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  Plane-wave Matrix Theory from N=4 Super Yang-Mills on
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mo ×
                        %msup
                          %mi S
                          %mn 3
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R} \times S^3
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0306054"} arXiv:hep-th/0306054
          %p
            Using the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-compactification"} KK-compactification
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%3D4+N%3D4+super+Yang-Mills+theory"} D=4 N=4 super Yang-Mills theory
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BMN+matrix+model"} BMN matrix model
            for
            = succeed "-computations" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lattice+gauge+theory"} lattice gauge theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%3D4+N%3D4+SYM"} D=4 N=4 SYM
            and for numerical checks of the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS-CFT+correspondence"} AdS-CFT correspondence
          %ul
            %li
              Masazumi Honda,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Goro+Ishiki"} Goro Ishiki
              = succeed "," do
                %em Direct test of the AdS/CFT correspondence by Monte Carlo studies of N=4 super Yang-Mills theory
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1308.3525"} arXiv:1308.3525
          %h3#planar_sector_integrability_mhv_amplitudes Planar sector, integrability, MHV amplitudes
          %p
            A comprehensive discussion of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integrability"} integrability
            related to anomalous dimension in the planar sector is in
          %ul#Beisert
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Niklas+Beisert"} Niklas Beisert
              et al.,
              %em Review of AdS/CFT Integrability, An Overview
              %p
                Lett. Math. Phys. vv, pp (2011), (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1012.3982"}> arXiv:1012.3982
                ).
          %p
            A review of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MHV+amplitudes"} MHV amplitudes
            is in
          %ul
            %li
              Gustavo Machado Monteiro,
              %em MHV Tree Amplitudes in Super-Yang-Mills and in Superstring Theory
              (2010) (
              %a{:href => "http://www.ift.unesp.br/posgrad/gustavo.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p
            Discussion of special properties of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scattering+amplitudes"} scattering amplitudes
            in the planar sector is in
          %ul#Arkani-Hamed
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nima+Arkani-Hamed"}> Nima Arkani-Hamed
              , Jacob L. Bourjaily, Freddy Cachazo, Alexander B. Goncharov, Alexander Postnikov, Jaroslav Trnka,
              %em Scattering Amplitudes and the Positive Grassmannian
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1212.5605"}> arXiv:1212.5605
              )
          %p For mathematical background see
          %ul
            %li
              Alexander Postnikov,
              %em Total positivity, Grassmannians, and networks
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0609764"}> arXiv:math/0609764
              )
          %h3#ReferencesTwistorSpace Twistor space formulation
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twistor"} twistor
            space formulation of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
